.\" Hand-written sections of improv-tui(1); crates/cli/src/man.rs adds the rest.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B improv-tui
shows one measure of a model as a pivot grid in the terminal: one category
down the rows, one across the columns, the rest as pages. Input cells are
edited in place; derived measures recompute incrementally as you type.
The model is saved when you quit.
.PP
A model is a store file made by
.BR improv (1),
or a Postgres model URL,
.BI postgres:// user @ host / db ?model= name\fR.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B arrows\fR, mouse click
Move the cell cursor.
.TP
.B Shift+arrows
Select a range; its sum shows in the status line.
.TP
.BR e ", " Enter
Edit the selected input cell, or the formula of a derived measure (it
accepts the symbolic form, \fBPrice * Quantity\fR, or the controlled English
the status line shows). Enter commits, Esc cancels; on an error the edit
stays open with the message under it. A formula that does not parse has
the offending token underlined in red, a
.B ^~~~
marker under it, the message, and a hint for the common mistakes: the
closest names to a misspelled one, a function's parameters when it got the
wrong number of arguments, the parenthesis left open. Left/Right, Home/End,
Backspace and Delete edit at the caret.
.TP
.B Tab \fR(in a formula)
Complete the name before the caret: a function (as
.IB NAME (\fR),
a measure or a category. One match completes; several extend to their
common prefix and list on the status line, and each further Tab puts the
next one in. While the caret is inside a call the status line shows its
signature, the current argument marked
.BR \(fopv\(fc ,
and at the end of the line the parameters still to type follow the caret,
dimmed.
.TP
.BR Tab ", " m
Show the next measure.
.TP
.B p
Pivot: rotate the axis order.
.TP
.BR [ " and " ]
Page through the page dimensions.
.TP
.BR f " / " F
Hide the cursor row's item / clear all filters.
.TP
.B S
Save the current layout as a view.
.TP
.B v
Cycle through the saved views.
.TP
.BR I " / " E
Import a CSV into a new measure / export the shown measure (a prompt opens).
.TP
.B R
Revert to the saved model, dropping this session's edits. Use it after a
save conflict, when another writer changed the model.
.TP
.B u
Undo the last change to the model: a cell, a formula, an import. Up to
50 changes are kept.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Redo the last change
.B u
undid. A new change drops what was undone.
.TP
.BR ? ", " F1
Open the function help: type to search the built-in functions, Up/Down and
PgUp/PgDn move through the results, and the selected function's signature,
category, aliases and description show below them. Enter inserts
.IB NAME (
into the cell being edited (F1 works while editing); Esc closes.
.TP
.B q
Quit and save.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
improv-tui sample.db
improv-tui 'postgres://me@127.0.0.1/sales?sslmode=disable&model=plan'
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Greg Burd <greg@burd.me>
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR improv (1),
.BR improv-files (5),
.BR improv-formulas (7),
.BR improv-gui (1),
.BR improv-server (1).
